BT. Then each active queue produces its HE, increments progress and completes at progress>=duration, inserting its residue. Clamp the total power to maxPower.","output_capacity":"Checked when starting only: empty output, no residue, or matching item+metadata with enough stack capacity. No recheck on completion if automation has changed the output.","is_on":"Any nonempty processing queue, even while storage is full; full storage does not pause/stop fuel processing.","queues":"Twelve independent persisted queues (progress, maxProgress, production and processing stack).","ports":"One source power port three blocks behind the core, determined by source orientation."}},"config":{"source":"src/main/java/com/hbm/config/VersatileConfig.java","decay":"enable528 || MachineConfig.doRTGsDecay","scale_power":"enable528 || MachineConfig.scaleRTGPower","defaults":{"doRTGsDecay":true,"scaleRTGPower":false},"lifespan":"RTGUtil.getLifespan uses 48000 ticks/day, 100 days/year here, float32 multiplication then long conversion; setDecays multiplies the long by 1.5 and converts back to long. External config overrides not applied."},"selection":"Source algorithm/fuel snapshot, no synthetic generic crafting duration or radiation-to-HE conversion.","runtime_gaps":[],"runtime_notes":["Native transactional runtime implemented; Manual and Automation use shared slot policy, inventory ports resolve to the core. Defaults match Java; optional global profiles are separate scope."],"coverage":{"machines":2,"rtg_pellets":10,"radgen_fuels":28,"skipped":0}}
